Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||12-29-2000||12:52 AM||||Isuzu<BR>getrag<BR>or 4spd (86 GT not 4.10)<P>motor of choice is zz4 355hp / 405 ft lbs torque , main objective , a few track events  and autocrosses , but mostly nasty stree machine<P>Thanks<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||12-29-2000||02:48 AM||||No tranny that ever came in the Fiero was designed to take 405 ft/lbs of torque.. The best choice would probably be the V6 4 speed.. cheaper to replace and from what I've heard the strongest.  If you plan to do a lot of street racing and power shifting I would keep a few spare tranny's on hand...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wannabe||12-29-2000||08:14 AM||||I've heard mixed reports on this, but only one first hand....the car has a 3800 s/c with nitrous, and so far so good. Does anybody have first hand experience of long term hard driving or racing with a v8 Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||12-29-2000||09:10 AM||||it's not 400 but mine had 310lbft and i never had anyproblems with it. (nitrous car)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6allgear.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6allgear.jpg</A>  and had 380ish in the shifts (at the wheels about 430 at the crank)  the only problem i had was killing weak clutches(4 of them)... the tranny never choked! Stock 86SE 4spd i then had the 4:10.. that was just CRAZY... 1,2 were a waste of time... but 3rd pulled like a train then 4th it fell on it's face.. (inadaquite HP)||||reg||1
Z||000004||BBBAD GT||12-29-2000||09:29 AM||||I have the Isuzu 5 speed in my V8 with no problems yet, but it only makes 207 rwhp.  The car did have a hot 350 in it (Chris is selling it in the Mall section) with the 4 speed munci, and the only problem he had was the dual friction clutch (std archie clutch)couldn't hold at high rpms.  Something to think about.  Centerforce said they could upgrade the clutch for $150 more (after their inspection of the same clutch, said nothing was wrong, just too much HP) to handle the HP.  <P>I'm curious, what kind of induction are you going with on top of the ZZ4?  I've seen a Fiero (Nytmare I think) with a ZZ4 and stock TPI pull about 260 rwhp.  If it were me, I wouldn't choke it with a stock TPI unit, and just put a carb with something like an RPM manifold on top, thats only of course if your  chassis can handle it, which is another topic....<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||12-29-2000||09:48 AM||||Do you have a budget?<P>I you can afford it, the VW 02A transaxle can be upgraded to take that kind of torque. The stock VW trans wouldn't hold it, but both Quaife (www.quaifeamerica.com) and Stealth Racing (www.stealthracing.co.uk) make six speed conversion kits for it.<BR>     I've corresponded with Quaife; they said that their street kit is rated for 275 ft lbs but can take more (probably wouldn't last long with 400 though).<BR>     I've also spoken with a gentleman at Stealth Racing who said that their kit is rated for over 400 ft lbs, and is being used by EIP Tuning behind 600HP turbo VW VR6's.<BR>     The Quaife kit is $2995 and the Stealth kit is 2000 (pounds) and the exchange rate sucks right now.<BR>     That, of course, is after you procure a junkyard 02A transaxle, and does not include installation.<BR>     And then you'd have to adapt it to the small block bolt pattern and figure out how to fit it in the chassis since it's longer than the Getrag.<BR>     But if you have the money to spend, it's a viable option||||reg||1
Z||000006||Verticalspeed||12-29-2000||01:14 PM|||| You will <B>break</B> any tranny if ABused. Your <B>weak link is the clutch itself</B> not the tranny. Getrags and others will break if you abuse them. It's all in the way you drive. Remember that the v8 fiero is not a "race car". I would drive it just as carefully as you would a normal 4 or v6 with ocasional spirited driving but don't do burnouts and clutch dumps. You will be dropping tha cradle all over again for a clutch and tranny replacement.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||12-29-2000||02:17 PM||||the thought of myself and my dad is a 6spd tranny froma celica ... Were waiting on diagrams of the tranny from a friend at toyota. I love my 4spd , but it's starting to wear it's 2nd gear syncros. I can get a isuzu trany and all related equip for $400 canadian... decisions decisions. I have always been amazed at my dads old L98 vette(87) it pulls like a freight train with 3.08 gears.. mid 5's to 60 , 14.03 in the 1/4.<P>as for induction .. I was initially going to go with a TPi for the clean look , but I have heard the "coke off" thing before. looked at accel superram , but too much $$$. perhaps a ported version of the tpi system with bigger injectors.<P>who knows....<P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000008||william_thorniii||12-29-2000||03:35 PM||||slammed,<P>When you get the info from Toyota I would greately appreciate it if you could send it my way.  I was told by CHR Fab to use the Supra trans, but hadn't had much time to do research.  <P>THX,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000009||Will||12-30-2000||05:22 PM||||I guess CHRFab isn't familiar with the Fiero. Supras are longitudinal.<BR>     Considering that the stock Celica engine makes about 130 ftlbs, I have series doubts that the Celica transaxle would survive 400+ ftlbs even as long as a Getrag.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||12-30-2000||05:56 PM||||if you had the cash i wonder if you could use a c5 corvette tranny. to give the new vettes 50-50 weight distribution the tranny is really a transaxle with the drive shaft bettween the engine and the tranny instead of the tranny and rear end. wonder if they can be hooked directly together? guess the engine would either be in the trunk or it would be your new center console though.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Will||12-31-2000||09:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>if you had the cash i wonder if you could use a c5 corvette tranny. to give the new vettes 50-50 weight distribution the tranny is really a transaxle with the drive shaft bettween the engine and the tranny instead of the tranny and rear end. wonder if they can be hooked directly together? guess the engine would either be in the trunk or it would be your new center console though.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you didn't mind losing your trunk, you could put the engine in the back and use a Smokey Yunick reverse rotation kit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Slammed Fiero||12-31-2000||03:15 PM||||After talking with a friend at TRD (toyota racing development)and his own personal research into the use of a celica tranny I have decided against it. Basically because they can't handle the torque. Steve millen has built a few 400 hp celica's with maybe 70% the torque of a stock zz4 and had transmission problems. Keep in mind the zz4 is 405ft lbs of torque in stock form. So back to the drawing board. I have been thinking of attempting to track down a HD (M82???) getrag from a Lumina Z34. Our tranny guy who built the transmission for my dads Corvair V8 and just finished the Tranny on our Impal SSized wagon (bigger servo's , high stall ...yadda yadda yadda) said he could build up the fiero transmission to be stronger , how much stronger is the question. I noticed archies old white IMSA f used a ZZ4 crate motor with TPI and a getrag. A lot of people have told me that the clutch is the weak link. A few engineers/ racers have told me that if I run sticky tires and the car hooks up something is bound to break. <P>I want to keep the set up of the car some what original , so a FWD tranny is a must... How long it will alst is the question....<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000013||MikeE||01-02-2001||07:51 AM||||Before you go with the Getrag 284 from any Z34, check out the performance 3.4 DOHC forum at <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/performance34dohc" TARGET=_blank>http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/performance34dohc</A>  and do a search.  Those guys are always complaining about how much trouble they have with that trans behind their modified 3.4s so I doubt if it will be better behind your engine.  Besides, they claim that GM does not sell rebuilt kits or replacement cases for that trans.  You apparently must send the trans in or buy a new one.  If that is true, then it's not worth the trouble of finding one.  A lot of them say they are switching to the 282 from a fiero due to the ease of finding replacement parts.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
